### =====================================================
### lin-spring-security-jwt - manual API test flow
### Start the app first: .\mvnw.cmd spring-boot:run
### =====================================================

@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Login as admin -> copy accessToken from the response
# @name adminLogin
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### 2. Login as normal user
# @name userLogin
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "user",
  "password": "user123"
}

### 3. Current user info (admin token) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4. List users - method level @PreAuthorize("hasAuthority('user:read')") (user token) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 5. Delete user - needs "user:write" (user token, only admin has it) -> 403
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/users/99
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 6. Delete user - admin token -> 400 (id 99 does not exist, but authorization passed)
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/users/99
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7. Admin stats - URL rule hasRole("ADMIN") (admin token) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8. Admin stats - URL rule hasRole("ADMIN") (user token) -> 403
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 9. Admin audit - method level hasAuthority('admin:read') (admin token) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 10. No token -> 401 with JSON body
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me

### 11. Tampered token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.tampered.token

### 12. Wrong password -> 401
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 13. Validation error -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "",
  "password": "x"
}

### =====================================================
### Slim token + Redis authority cache (Plan B)
### Prerequisite: Redis running on localhost:6379
###   docker run -d --name redis -p 6379:6379 redis:7
### Inspect cache with: redis-cli GET auth:authorities:admin
### =====================================================

### 14. Token stays slim - decode the middle segment, only sub/iat/exp inside
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 15. Evict authority cache for 'user' (permission changes take effect on next request)
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/admin/authority-cache/user
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 16. Permission revocation demo:
###  a) open H2 console, run: DELETE FROM user_roles WHERE user_id = (SELECT id FROM users WHERE username='user')
###  b) GET /users with the user token -> still 200 (cached authorities)
###  c) run request 15 above to evict
###  d) run this request again -> 403 (authorities reloaded from DB, now empty)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
